            <ArticleTitle>[Haematogenous osteomyelitis as a differential diagnosis for knee pain in a ten-year-old girl].</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">V09150725</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Knee pain is a frequent symptom facing the general practitioner. Some of the more severe differential diagnoses include bone infections and malignancy. We present a case report of a ten-year-old sports active and otherwise healthy girl with knee pain, which turned out to be haematogenous osteomyelitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
